                <pb facs="0966" n="850" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg850"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/114.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 23, 1 p.m. General Villa declines to deliver body of Benton
                    but states that he will permit his widow or relatives to visit the cemetery in
                    company with any representative who may be designated by our Government and that
                    for their benefit he will order exhumation of body which will then be reinterred
                    in the same place where it now lies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
